course: dictionary
lesson: 1149
title: Finding meaning from context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Context means the words and sentences around a new word. They often give clues to its meaning. «If the smoke alarm sounds for a real fire: get out, stay out, and call the fire brigade.» You call for help in a real fire, so a fire brigade must be the group who comes to put out the fire.
explain: Now test your idea. Swap in a simple word: «call the fire team» still makes sense, so you are on the right track. Brigade means a group of people who do a job together. Some brigades are parts of an army, made of soldiers, but the fire brigade is a team of firefighters.
explain: Look at the clues in another sentence: «fire brigades use similar machines to reach high windows.» Machines and high windows tell you the brigade is a team with equipment for rescue work. Read the whole text, check the clues, then decide.
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Brigade can also be a joke, as in «the umbrella brigade», which means a group of people with the same opinion. Context tells you which meaning the writer means, so always read the sentence before you decide.
fact: A brigade is a big group of soldiers, part of an army.
fact: A brigade is an organised group of people who do a job together, like a fire brigade.
fact: «Fire brigade» means the team of firefighters you call in an emergency.
fact: «In 1666 the Great Fire of London burned much of the City for four days; afterwards... fire brigades grew.»
fact: Jokingly, «the umbrella brigade» means a group of people with the same opinion.
exercise: «Call the fire brigade in an emergency.» What is a fire brigade? | A brick building for storing water | *A team of firefighters you call in an emergency | A tall ladder for street lights | A kind of fire made of wood
exercise: «Fire brigades use similar machines to reach high windows.» Which word in this sentence means a team that does a job together? | windows | high | machines | *fire brigades
exercise: Jokes: «Everyone at the party was in the umbrella brigade.» What does brigade mean here? | A big group of soldiers, part of an army | *A group of people with the same opinion | A fire engine | A ladder for reaching windows
test: «In 1666 the Great Fire of London burned much of the City for four days.» According to the sentence, what grew afterwards? | Carbon monoxide alarms | Tall castles | *Fire brigades | Cherry pickers
test: «The brigade of soldiers marched across the field.» What is a brigade in this sentence? | A jokey group of people with umbrellas | A kind of fire engine | *A big group of soldiers, part of an army | A small wooden hut
exam: «Call the fire brigade.» What does brigade mean in this phrase? | A brick building | A tall ladder | *A team of firefighters you call in an emergency | A kind of fire made of wood
